# Lichess API (ChessHub)

Follow the **lichess-api** skill and `Lichessorg API reference.json` (v2.0.153).

## Must follow

- Base URL: `https://lichess.org` (API paths under `/api/...` unless the OpenAPI says otherwise).
- **Serialize** outbound Lichess HTTP calls (one at a time). On **429**, wait ≥ 1 minute and reduce frequency.
- Send `User-Agent: ChessHub/1.0 (tournament platform)` (or extend that string — do not drop it).
- Tokens and PKCE verifiers: **server-only**. Never expose in client bundles or URLs.
- OAuth: Authorization Code + **PKCE S256** only. No refresh tokens. Support token strings ≥ 512 chars matching `^[A-Za-z0-9_]+$`.
- ChessHub account linking uses: `email:read preference:read tournament:write`.
- Tournament **results** (`/api/tournament/{id}/results`, `/api/swiss/{id}/results`): `Accept: application/x-ndjson`; parse with `parseLichessNdjson`. Import prizes only when the event is **finished**.

## Prefer existing helpers

- `src/lib/server/chess/lichess.js` — OAuth, account, public ratings
- `src/lib/server/chess/lichess-tournaments.js` — Arena create (rated), ID normalize, finish check, standings, prize match

```js
// ❌ BAD — parallel bursts / inventing clients
await Promise.all(ids.map((id) => fetch(`https://lichess.org/api/tournament/${id}`)));

// ✅ GOOD — reuse helpers, sequential, finished-only results
const standings = await fetchLichessTournamentStandings(id, 'arena');
```

## Out of scope for prize import

Do not treat team-battle awards, simuls, studies, or OTB manual scores as supported Lichess prize sources unless product explicitly expands support.
